course: dictionary
lesson: 3096
title: Effort: hard work, a try, and a force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Effort means the hard work and energy you put into doing something. «Celebrating everyone's effort after SATs is good, because results are not the only thing that counts.» Here effort means the hard work you do, even when the result is not perfect.
explain: An effort can also be one try at something. «Make an effort» means try hard to do it. Context tells you which meaning to use: in «a team effort», people work together, so effort means the work they all do.
explain: In science, effort is the force you push or pull with on a lever or machine to move a load. A small effort can move a big load. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: if «effort» fits as hard work, you have the right meaning.
fact: Effort meaning hard work is uncountable, so we say «a lot of effort», not «an effort», when we mean the hard work itself.
fact: «Respect is earned by effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.»
fact: At school, people often praise effort, as in «great effort!», even when the result is not perfect.
fact: Useful phrases: «make an effort» means try hard, «worth the effort» means worth the work, and «with no effort» means easily.
fact: In science, a lever lets a small effort move a big load.
exercise: «Celebrating everyone's effort after SATs is good, because results are not the only thing that counts.» In this sentence, what does effort mean? | A prize | *Hard work and trying your best | A loud noise | A test score
exercise: «The best compliments are about things people choose or do: a drawing, a goal, their kindness, their effort, a tasty meal.» Which thing in this list is something a person does or chooses? | Their height | *Their effort | Their age | Their eye colour
exercise: Max says, «I'll make an effort to finish my drawing.» What does make an effort mean? | Draw on the wall | Stop trying | Sleep until lunch | *Try hard to do it
test: «Respect is earned by effort, skill, honesty, kindness and courage.» Which of these does respect NOT come from? | Honesty | Courage | Effort | *Making people afraid of you
test: In science, what is effort? | The load that gets moved | A lever | *The force you put on a lever or machine to move a load | The name of a machine
exam: Lily says, «It was a team effort.» What does she mean? | A broken machine | One person working alone | A test with no marks | *People working together
